# The product of two balls with one-limb centers: |xy - cx cy| <= |cx| ry + |cy| rx + rx ry, plus
# the error of the rounded center product, at most U |cz| + V from the claims of mul_1_1.
kernel:        ball_mul_1
input:         cx
input:         rx
input:         cy
input:         ry
output:        cz
output:        rz
value:         cx*cy
requires:      nonneg rx
requires:      nonneg ry
ensures:       encloses cz rz x*y x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
source:        midpoint-radius product (Milestone 1 listing)
status:        unverified
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

cz = prod(cx, cy)
ax = abs(cx)
ay = abs(cy)
t1 = rmul(ax, ry)
t2 = rmul(ay, rx)
t3 = rmul(rx, ry)
s1 = radd(t1, t2)
s2 = radd(s1, t3)
mz = abs(cz)
d0 = rmul(const unit_computed(mul_1_1), mz)
d  = radd(d0, const tiny_computed(mul_1_1))
rz = radd(s2, d)
